## 2. Key Files & Structure

```
/cv
├── CLAUDE.md                           # Project instructions (read first)
├── AGENTS.md                           # This file - agent context
├── config.yaml                         # User config (gitignored) - has URLs, paths
├── config.example.yaml                 # Template config
│
├── sources/                            # INPUT: Raw materials
│   ├── current-cv/[NAME].pdf           # Original CV
│   ├── linkedin/                       # LinkedIn export PDFs
│   └── blog-cache/                     # Cached blog posts as markdown
│
├── analysis/                           # Research & findings
│   ├── achievements/achievements.md    # Main achievement database
│   ├── skills-inventory/skills.md      # Comprehensive skills by category
│   ├── blog-analysis.md                # Blog content analysis
│   ├── cv-review.md                    # Original CV analysis
│   ├── git-analysis.md                 # Repository commit analysis
│   └── linkedin-analysis.md            # LinkedIn profile analysis
│
├── outputs/                            # Generated materials
│   ├── cv-versions/
│   │   ├── [role-1].md
│   │   ├── [role-2].md
│   │   └── [role-3].md
│   └── linkedin-updates/
│       └── recommendations.md
│
└── .beads/                             # Task tracking (bd commands)
```

### Config File (config.yaml)
```yaml
blog_url: "[YOUR BLOG URL]"
github_username: "[YOUR USERNAME]"
linkedin_url: "[YOUR LINKEDIN URL]"
repositories:
  - path: "[PATH TO YOUR MAIN REPO]"
```

